.TH QFW-SERVICE-START 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-service-start \- low-level launcher for one QFw service process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-service-start
.BI --service-id " id"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-service-start
starts one named QFw service process, waits for service readiness and required
directory registration, and writes PID and readiness records. It is retained
for compatibility and is used by the
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1)
lifecycle engine. Administrators normally use that manager instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --service-id " id"
Select one manifest service. This option is required.
.TP
.BI --site-config " file"
Select the site manifest, directory connection, device-access path, and QPM
settings.
.TP
.BI --module " module"
Override the service module for low-level integration.
.TP
.BI --load-modules " modules"
Override the comma-separated DEFw module load list.
.TP
.BI --operation-mode " mode"
Set the QPM operation mode. The default is
.BR long-running .
.TP
.BI --run-dir " directory"
Use an explicit component run directory.
.TP
.BI --listen-port " port"
Set the service port. The default is 8290.
.TP
.BI --telnet-port " port"
Set the diagnostic port. The default is 8291.
.TP
.BI --timeout " seconds"
Override the directory-registration and readiness timeout.
.TP
.BI --pid-file " file"
Write the process identifier to an explicit file.
.TP
.BI --ready-file " file"
Write readiness JSON to an explicit file.
.TP
.B --background
Return after readiness while leaving the process running.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Write representative state without starting a process.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1),
.BR qfw-dirsvc-start (1),
.BR qfw-services.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-site.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-service-plane (7)
